<worksheet >
    <title>VS-1 Vector Spaces and Subspaces</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete both problems. 
      Complete one problem with progress on the other to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
    <exercise>
        <p>Let <m>V</m> be the set of all vectors in <m>\mathbb{R}^3</m>  with normal 
          vector addition and the scalar multiplication defined as 
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1">
      <mrow>k\begin{bmatrix}x\\y\\z\end{bmatrix}= \begin{bmatrix}1\\1\\1\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
    </md> for <m>k \in \mathbb{R}</m>.</p><p>Determine if <m>V</m> is a 
              vector space. If it is, verify the axioms. If it is not, identify 
              which axiom(s) fail and provide a counterexample to show that the 
              axiom(s) fail.</p>
    </exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise>
        <p>Let <m>V=M_{23}</m>, the set of all <m>2\times 3</m> matrices with normal matrix 
          addition and scalar multiplication.  Let <m>H</m> be the set of all 
          <m>2\times 3</m> matrices of the form
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
      <mrow>\begin{bmatrix}a &amp; b &amp; c\\ d &amp; e &amp; f\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
    </md> where <m>b = c^2</m>. Determine if <m>H</m> is a subspace of <m>V</m>. 
            Justify your answer.</p>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>